00:20:04,678 --> 00:20:07,321
So there's Carl, Aya and Hus.

236
00:20:07,602 --> 00:20:08,663
Put your hand up, Hus, please.

237
00:20:08,743 --> 00:20:10,326
There we are, you see.

238
00:20:10,906 --> 00:20:13,971
So it'd be nice to have that, you see.

239
00:20:13,951 --> 00:20:19,782
And hopefully to find a way to run this place which doesn't depend on me.

240
00:20:20,022 --> 00:20:22,228
That's my target for the next five years.

241
00:20:23,770 --> 00:20:24,532
And then I'll disappear.

242
00:20:29,462 --> 00:20:31,487
Yeah, that would be my hope anyway.

243
00:20:35,922 --> 00:20:41,709
I was going to say disappear in what respect, as in go somewhere else, as in just... No, just no.

244
00:20:42,249 --> 00:20:42,710
I don't think...

245
00:20:42,769 --> 00:20:44,412
I'll only disappear when it's time to go.

246
00:20:47,955 --> 00:21:03,094
I'm wondering about the... You talked before about Gaia House and the dilemma of becoming a layperson and disrobing, and it's quite a new... Well, I suppose we think of

247
00:21:03,292 --> 00:21:27,798
monks within a group and you've chosen to be on your own i just wonder about your commitment to being in robes and just sticking with the monastic order despite but not being with other people yeah yeah yeah um no that's true lone monks are known you don't not you know you will get monks who are quite happy to be on their own um it's not a choice it's just the way i've ended up

248
00:21:27,778 --> 00:21:35,071
There are no Western monks that I was involved with in Sri Lanka who could have come over with me.

249
00:21:35,432 --> 00:21:36,213
There just weren't any.

250
00:21:36,694 --> 00:21:37,296
That's the end of it.

251
00:21:37,416 --> 00:21:42,306
So I was basically on my own from the beginning, you see.

252
00:21:42,665 --> 00:21:49,077
It would have been nice to have had a partner or somebody to run the place, you know, somebody whom you're compatible with.

253
00:21:49,902 --> 00:21:53,406
You have to remember that just because you're a monk doesn't mean you like the person.

254
00:21:53,586 --> 00:21:56,932
It's a varied community.

255
00:21:58,835 --> 00:22:04,884
But there have been many times throughout the 30 years, this is my 30th year, where I've wanted to leave.

256
00:22:05,644 --> 00:22:10,432
There was one point where I was going to bed saying, right, tomorrow that's it, we'll get out, we'll do something useful.

257
00:22:10,712 --> 00:22:13,236
And I'd wake up in the morning and I'd say, well, God, I'll give you just one more day.

258
00:22:13,836 --> 00:22:15,640
And in the end I just had to laugh.

259
00:22:15,619 --> 00:22:21,531
Now, every time I came to this point of wanting to leave, I couldn't think of anything at all in society that attracted me.

260
00:22:21,893 --> 00:22:22,795
I went through the whole job.

261
00:22:23,076 --> 00:22:28,287
And I usually ended up with a fantasy of stacking shelves and going back to the garret and doing my meditation.

262
00:22:28,728 --> 00:22:30,431
So I said, well, I can do that without stacking shelves.

263
00:22:34,239 --> 00:22:35,181
So I never left.

264
00:22:35,666 --> 00:22:39,750
Every time that, you know, there were times when I was very close.

265
00:22:40,491 --> 00:22:43,994
One of them was at the end of that escapade up in North London.

266
00:22:44,414 --> 00:22:47,738
I mean, that was an obvious time where, you know, I didn't know where to go.

267
00:22:48,199 --> 00:22:50,800
There was nowhere, but I just, there was nothing.

268
00:22:50,941 --> 00:22:54,585
I just ended up faffing about.

269
00:22:56,326 --> 00:22:57,027
What about the robes?

270
00:22:57,047 --> 00:23:01,111
What about the actual... Robes?

271
00:23:01,590 --> 00:23:03,413
Well, I'm stuck with the colour.

272
00:23:04,134 --> 00:23:09,522
I mean, I'd love to wear blue.

273
00:23:09,663 --> 00:23:10,545
You know, pink.

274
00:23:10,785 --> 00:23:11,506
I'd love to wear pink.

275
00:23:12,407 --> 00:23:13,128
You look pink.

276
00:23:13,869 --> 00:23:14,230
Pink-like.

277
00:23:14,851 --> 00:23:16,773
What do you mean by the robes?

278
00:23:16,954 --> 00:23:21,842
Well, I suppose, why not just become a layperson?

279
00:23:21,942 --> 00:23:22,323
Oh, I see.

280
00:23:22,702 --> 00:23:22,884
Ah.

281
00:23:23,944 --> 00:23:24,786
Oh, very good.

