00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:43,744
What's your funniest teaching experience?

321
00:27:43,765 --> 00:27:45,047
Funniest teaching experience?

322
00:27:45,928 --> 00:27:47,150
Can't think of any.

323
00:27:47,170 --> 00:27:49,393
What do you mean by funniest teaching experience?

324
00:27:49,413 --> 00:27:51,455
Actually, you've got a question to answer as well.

325
00:27:52,857 --> 00:27:55,161
You answer her question.

326
00:27:55,340 --> 00:27:56,242
That was about the robes.

327
00:27:56,903 --> 00:27:57,505
See, I remembered.

328
00:27:58,826 --> 00:28:00,008
The robes.

329
00:28:00,375 --> 00:28:01,837
Why don't I?

330
00:28:01,978 --> 00:28:02,459
Oh, I see.

331
00:28:03,019 --> 00:28:05,644
Well, the robes are a guardian, really.

332
00:28:05,663 --> 00:28:09,429
Because, you know, you have to behave in a certain way when you walk around in robes.

333
00:28:10,631 --> 00:28:12,534
But it's just, you just get used to it.

334
00:28:12,934 --> 00:28:14,317
I haven't even thought about that, really.

335
00:28:14,356 --> 00:28:25,512
The question was about, you know, other than that, you know, have you thought about being a Dharma teacher, but as a layperson?

336
00:28:25,953 --> 00:28:26,294
Oh, yeah.

337
00:28:26,413 --> 00:28:30,180
That's what I thought, yeah, but it doesn't attract me because...

338
00:28:31,138 --> 00:28:37,330
Dharma teachers, they get support, but remember they've got massive overheads.

339
00:28:38,113 --> 00:28:44,064
Sometimes they have children, they have cars to run, all that sort of stuff.

340
00:28:44,085 --> 00:28:47,751
Being a monk really releases me from all that sort of baggage.

341
00:28:48,272 --> 00:28:52,961
You shouldn't call it baggage really, you should call it delight.

342
00:28:54,712 --> 00:28:57,036
Releases me from the delight of all my life.

343
00:28:58,818 --> 00:29:05,428
So that my, you know, once I've got my laptop and stuff like that, that's it.

344
00:29:06,930 --> 00:29:12,998
If I left, it would, I don't know, it just doesn't attract me.

345
00:29:13,699 --> 00:29:15,060
I mean, I'm conditioned now.

346
00:29:15,741 --> 00:29:18,005
It takes such a long time to recondition yourself.

347
00:29:18,586 --> 00:29:21,349
I just feel comfortable in the roads.

348
00:29:21,971 --> 00:29:22,711
It's as simple as that.

349
00:29:24,076 --> 00:29:25,337
And I haven't got long to go anyway.

350
00:29:26,559 --> 00:29:28,342
That's the point that you... Ah!

